ROOT CAUSE (code-level, not a seeder/data-shape defect):
VendorApp/lib/features/order/screens/order_details_screen.dart:415 --
  if (order.deliveryAddress != null || (order.deliveryInstruction!.isNotEmpty || order.deliveryInstruction != null)) ...
Operator precedence/ordering bug: the RHS force-unwraps `order.deliveryInstruction!` BEFORE the
null check that appears later in the same clause (`order.deliveryInstruction != null`) -- so when
deliveryAddress is null AND deliveryInstruction is null, the `!` throws instead of short-circuiting
safely. This is a pre-existing bug in the Delivery-Info card, unrelated to prescription_order
handling (the AC's own stated risk area) -- it fires for ANY order with an absent delivery address
AND absent delivery instruction, which is the normal, correct shape for a take_away/self-pickup
order (no delivery address is expected for pickup). NEARS-3499's seeded order is store_id=1,
order_type=take_away, order_status=handover, cash_on_delivery, prescription_order=1 -- the first
take_away order this vendor's order-detail screen has been driven against live, which is why this
was never previously observed on device.

IMPACT: the screen's GetBuilder rebuild throws during the Delivery-Info section build; verified via
accessibility dump immediately after tap -- 12 nodes total, only the app-bar title/status text
render ("Order #91369", "Order is Ready For Handover"); the entire body (order items, delivery
info, billing summary, and the camera/gallery picker control this AC needs to reach) never paints.

This blocks NEARS-3499 AC5 (order-detail camera/gallery picker reachable) -- the screen never
renders far enough to expose the picker control, regardless of the prescription_order=1 /
order_details-fetch-skip path the AC text specifically asked to confirm is clean (that specific
skip path is NOT what crashes here -- this is an unrelated, earlier crash in the same screen's
